Loop Resample for Maya 0.2.2

Version 0.2.1 fixes native-window mouse events being treated as outside
clicks, which incorrectly cancelled Alt+mouse viewport navigation.
Input ownership is now handled only on the QWidget dispatch stage.

Based on Loop Resample for Blender 1.0.3 by YLIANG.
Original project: https://github.com/YLIANG021/Loop-Resample
Original license: GPL-3.0-or-later (blender_manifest.toml).

This Maya adaptation is licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later.
The centripetal Catmull-Rom, source-density/even sampling, Taubin smoothing,
and monotone strip reconstruction follow the original project's design.
Host integration, conservative topology/attribute transfer, Qt dialog,
Maya undo command, installer and regression tests have been rewritten.
This is an independent, partial port, not an official YLIANG release.
It does not reproduce the original Blender planner and modal viewport UI
exactly. There is no warranty of fitness for production assets.

Maya 2019/2020 and their bundled APIs/Qt are runtime prerequisites supplied
by Autodesk; they are not included in this distribution. No Autodesk SDK
headers, libraries, or binaries are redistributed.

Supported: simple open/closed edge paths, single-row triangle/quad strips,
triangle fans, simple polygon caps, multi-path common delta, smoothing,
even spacing, face-corner UV sets, face materials and hard edges.

Unsupported inputs are rejected: construction history/deformers/skin,
instances, referenced or locked meshes, downstream geometry connections,
color sets, locked normals, crease weights, mesh blind data, component sets,
branched selections and polygons with holes.
UV/material/hard-edge boundaries are conservatively pinned. Reducing below
the number of required anchors is rejected rather than silently losing them.
Complex strip layouts may be rejected. There is no global surface collision
detection, no per-frame local-patch acceleration, and no custom normal/skin/color
interpolation. Vertex/face/UV IDs may change.
Try on a saved duplicate; inspect the result before committing it to an asset.

Version 0.2.2: a single Loop Resample menu item starts viewport interaction.
The panel menu item and new shelf creation have been removed. Reinstallation
removes only the legacy plugin-owned shelf buttons; other shelf contents stay.
If the old dedicated shelf becomes empty, Maya asks whether to delete its tab.
Wheel: segment delta; Shift+Wheel: smooth; Ctrl+Wheel: even; R: reset.
Left click/Enter: commit once; right click/Esc: restore the original mesh.
Alt+mouse navigation passes through to Maya. The viewport HUD is mouse-transparent.
Changing tool/selection, leaving the viewport for other UI, switching apps,
or saving/opening a scene cancels the preview. Other modeling hotkeys are blocked
while the tool owns the viewport.
Restart Maya after replacing files to avoid mixing cached Python module versions.

The native space hotbox and main Edit Mesh menu include one Loop Resample
viewport entry. Installation enables auto-load for this plugin only.
No space hotkey, marking-menu slot, menu-set visibility, userSetup or Autodesk
installation script is changed. If the Modeling/Edit Mesh row is hidden in
your hotbox preferences, use Hotbox Controls to show Modeling menus yourself.
Plugin unload removes only menu items tagged as owned by Loop Resample.
